---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Prateek Mittal"
  description="Personal biography, background, and perspectives of Prateek Mittal."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 sm:py-20 space-y-12">
    
    <!-- Header with Portrait -->
    <div class="flex flex-col-reverse sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-6 pb-2">
      <div class="space-y-1">
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 tracking-tight">
          About Me
        </h1>
        <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans text-sm">
          A bit more about my background, work, and interests.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="w-24 h-24 sm:w-28 sm:h-28 rounded-full overflow-hidden border-2 border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 shadow-sm flex-shrink-0">
        <img
          src="/images/prateek.png"
          alt="Prateek Mittal"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Long-form Personal Essay -->
    <div class="space-y-6 font-serif text-lg text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-relaxed border-t border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 pt-8">
      <p>
        I have always felt that mathematics, social conscience, and poetry are not separate endeavors, but three dialects of the same quiet search for clarity.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-4">
        Pratigya Abhiyan & The Grassroots
      </h2>
      <p>
        During my undergraduate studies in computer engineering at Thapar Institute, I walked into a classroom run by <strong>Pratigya Abhiyan</strong>. What started as an evening volunteering commitment became four defining years of my life. 
      </p>
      <p>
        Teaching children of daily-wage workers and migrant families stripped away any naive romanticism about technology. I realized that the hardest part of education isn't explaining complex theorems; it's earning the trust of a child whose life has offered them very little stability. Serving as Academic Head taught me how to design curricula that met children where they were, how to mentor fellow university volunteers, and how to stay grounded in real human needs.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-4">
        Research & Medical Intelligence
      </h2>
      <p>
        In research, I work on problems where geometry and statistical theory help us see biology more clearly. With the <strong>VEDAs Lab</strong> and my co-authors, this has led to five accepted contributions at <strong>MICCAI 2026</strong> (including three oral presentations and the Society Travel Grant) and theoretical work on robust high-dimensional estimation in <strong>TMLR</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        At <strong>Yale University</strong>, I was fortunate to contribute to <strong>BrainLM</strong> (ICLR 2024)—a foundation model trained on 6,700 hours of whole-brain fMRI recordings to decode human cognitive states from non-invasive functional imaging.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-4">
        Industry & Healthcare Ethics
      </h2>
      <p>
        In industry, I work as an AI Decision Science Analyst within <strong>Accenture Strategy & Consulting</strong>'s AI & Data ecosystem. Previously at <strong>Dr. Lal PathLabs</strong>, I built clinical GenAI pipelines, automated document intelligence, and designed unified risk scoring frameworks tailored to Indian reference intervals.
      </p>
      <p>
        Recognizing that rapid algorithmic deployment often leaves patient safety behind, I founded the <strong>Foundation for Ethical AI in Healthcare</strong>—a Section 8 initiative aimed at bridging the regulatory and accountability gap for clinical algorithms in India.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-4">
        Poetry & The Quiet Hours
      </h2>
      <p>
        When work is done, I write poetry in Hindi and English. My writing revolves around themes of <em>भीतर का ठिकाना</em> (the inner refuge) and <em>क्षीर-नीर विवेक</em> (the classical philosophical ideal of separating essence from noise). It is how I stay quiet, thoughtful, and human.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Contact & Conversation -->
    <div class="border-t border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 pt-8 space-y-3 font-sans text-sm text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">
      <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50">
        Get in touch
      </h3>
      <p>
        I enjoy conversations about medical AI, clinical ethics, grassroots education, and poetry. Feel free to reach out directly at <a href="mailto:prateekmittal154@gmail.com" class="text-terracotta-500 hover:underline">prateekmittal154@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
